# kin/youth/legs/tips: the youth's shoe tips under a long hem (robe, gown, kaftan, wrap)
# THE SIDE WALK AND RUN (KIN-YOUTH, P2b motion rollout 2026-10-22): each side walk / run tip is std's and far's boot of the
# key at the same placement (the leg kit writes both), windowed to the part that shows under a long hem (this part draws
# over the hem's under-edge): the planted Y0 whole, the heel-strike Y1's heel end (cols 0-3), the heel-off Y2's and the
# toe-off Y3's toe end (3-5, 2-4), the flight's pointed Y9's toe end (0-3); the near boot first, the far under it. In the
# flight both feet show under the raised skirt.
# History (superseded for the side walk and run):
# THE SIDE WALK AND RUN (the motion rebuild, 2026-10-21, docs/MOTION_P2.md 7.4): each side walk / run tip is the boot of
# std.pxm's key at the same placement (boots_youth.stamps), windowed to the stamp's columns (`put <key> <dx> <dy> [under]
# cols <a>-<b>`): Y0 and Y1 whole, Y2 its toe end (cols 3-5 R), Y3 its toe (2-4 on the ground, 3-4 lifted 1: the walk
# pass's swing toe ahead at +6, motion fix round 3); the run's lifted feet (push, flight) stay under the skirt.
# History (superseded for the side walk and run by the rebuild above; front and back keys, the idles and the other
# keys are unchanged):
# kin/youth/legs/tips: the youth's shoe tips under a long hem (robe, gown, kaftan, wrap): drawn over the hem's under-edge
# KIN-YOUTH (P2b wave 2). Format: rpg/art/doll/doll.h. Each drawing is the lower toe row and the sole of the youth's
# own boots in the same key (legs/std), so the tips stand, step and lift exactly where the legs would: both shoes show
# in every front and back frame, a lifted shoe rises a row over the hem, the run's flight lifts both; seated and
# cross-legged the toes peek under the skirt. Regions: B shoe, O sole.
use person
body youth
role legs tips
layer hangFront
anchor pivot
keys legs
z 9
stamps boots_youth
tags boots-stamped

